# Public App Setting navigation readiness — read-only causal review

Reviewed the actual additional public combined probe on candidate `c3ae5adbc06eea2740aba3d62492ea001c1c0da0`. This was an additional imported original test plus an external afterEach Storage journey. The original imported first case failed at application-platform.spec.ts:111. The afterEach continued after the failure, so its final page/error-context is not evidence of the DOM at the failing assertion.

**Confirmed cause in this trace:** the new test's Save helper considers the removed form sufficient readiness for the destination resource page. The form can correctly close after accepted command processing while the normal asynchronous Next router navigation is still pending. The immediate strict `.portal-properties` assertion therefore runs on the legitimate Web App Overview, which intentionally contains two distinct definition lists: configuration and configuration analysis. This is not evidence of duplicated pages or a hydration duplicate.

