The first destination snapshot occurs during the external afterEach's service-navigation preparation. Its presence proves that the requested destination did arrive without a source change or retry; it does not make the earlier original assertion a pass. Later Storage pages must not be substituted for these snapshots.

The actual accepted receipt and the new row in revision5 rule out a fabricated success or lost resource in this case. This is temporary client-owned/replay-checked simulation evidence, not a persistent PostgreSQL commit claim.

## Source order at c3ae5ad

- tests/e2e/application-platform.spec.ts:42–51 awaits the accepted original command response and `.lab-form` count0, then returns. It does not await the destination's actual title/identity.
- src/features/laboratory/laboratory.tsx:300–308 accepts the result and clears parent form/preview state; lines309–355 derive the real created ID and call `router.push` to `appSetting` for the actual new setting. Next router.push is asynchronous and does not return a destination-render promise.
- src/features/laboratory/application.tsx:288–292 closes the editor after the accepted commit promise resolves. That promise confirms accepted processing, not completion of the later client route.
- The Web App Overview intentionally renders its configuration PropertyList and its separate model/workspace/revision-bound analysis PropertyList. On the actual setting destination, exactly one setting PropertyList is rendered.

## Bounded correction recommendation

Before the existing first case's unchanged line111 assertion, assert the actual destination heading `APP_MODE` with the original `.portal-title h1` locator. Retain the strict original `.portal-properties` assertion and its expected`synthetic` value byte-for-byte. This adds missing destination-readiness coverage without choosing a first match, narrowing away duplicates, adding sleeps, changing timeouts/retries or changing product behavior. The destination ID and original receipt in this trace independently confirm that APP_MODE is the actual created setting, not an arbitrary convenient heading.

The corrected control still fails if the destination never arrives, the wrong resource arrives, two title nodes remain, the setting value is absent, or duplicate properties lists remain on the setting page. It does not mask a duplicated UI.

This review makes no claim that older unrelated Compute/Back/Axe/landing failures are fixed. It explains only this concrete new additional-public-probe failure. The original red execution and ZIP must remain recorded; a subsequent pass cannot be relabelled as an original pass. No product, test, documentation, release record, stamp, server or Git ref was changed by this investigation.
